drowzeys/TensorFold (a TensorFold fork)
  https://github.com/drowzeys/TensorFold (branch glm-moe-dsa-tp4, commit befd47d)
  By drowzeys. Apache License, Version 2.0.
  patches/0106-glm-full-prompt-experts.patch: tensorfold/cuda/exl3/prompt_experts.cu, prompt_experts.cpp and
  prompt_experts.py are that fork's files (by drowzeys; their design adapted, as their header says, from the
  GLM-5.3-Flash recipe's prompt kernels), modified: a pairs mode (the down kernel stores each routed pair's
  unweighted output row into a [pairs, D] buffer, without zeroing or atomics; the caller adds the slots in slot
  order), the extension renamed, the trellis row stride taken from the expert width (TensorFold v0.6.0 has no
  gu_stride), an fp16 buffer that may be lent (PromptScratch's xd). The headers of prompt_experts.cu and
  prompt_experts.py say what changed.

